      <div class="accent-line"></div>
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.4rem);font-weight:300;color:#fff;margin-bottom:1rem;">Activewear Shipping and Logistics</h2>
    </div>

    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;">
      Bangladesh's strategic location provides efficient shipping options for activewear exports to global markets. For European Union buyers, sea freight from Chittagong Port takes 22-28 days to major European ports including Rotterdam, Hamburg, and Antwerp. Duty-free access under EBA until November 2026 provides additional 12% savings on import duties compared to other manufacturing destinations. This combination of competitive FOB pricing and duty-free access makes Bangladesh the lowest total landed cost option for EU buyers seeking activewear production.
    </p>

    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-top:1.5rem;">
      For United States buyers, sea freight to US East Coast ports (New York, Savannah, Charleston) takes 30-40 days, while US West Coast ports (Los Angeles, Long Beach) take 40-50 days. Bangladesh avoids Section 301 tariffs that add 25% to Chinese imports, providing significant duty savings on activewear imports. Air freight is available for urgent orders, with 5-7 day transit times to major US and European airports, though air freight costs 5-8 times more than sea freight and is typically used only for sample shipments or urgent replenishment orders.
    </p>

    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-top:1.5rem;">
      Every activewear shipment leaves our factory with a complete export document package: commercial invoice, packing list, certificate of origin, and OEKO-TEX certification documentation where applicable. Our logistics team liaises directly with freight forwarders to keep customs clearance moving. We quote under EXW, FOB, or CIF incoterms, whichever suits your supply chain — FOB is the most requested since it puts freight and carrier selection in your hands, while CIF folds freight and insurance into our price for buyers who prefer a single landed-cost figure.
    </p>
